/*--- Choupo stream state.  Every DIMENSIONAL value carries its unit; the parser converts to SI.
     componentMolarFlows is the OVERALL material (all phases); a phases{} block, when present,
     is a decomposition that sums back to it exactly. ---*/

/*  AN INITIAL GUESS, NOT AN INPUT -- the same status as 0/distillate.

    Seeded from the paper's MEASURED bottoms composition (Table 2), but scaled
    to the rate the ENGINE will produce, B = F - D = 452.710957 - 142.023556 =
    310.687401 kmol/h.  The paper's own 18119 kg/h corresponds to 311.208528
    kmol/h at its measured bottoms composition -- 0.17 % more.  That gap is the
    tables' rounding, argued in flowsheetDict section 6; it is not reconciled
    here, and the bottoms rate is NOT a case input.

    The i-butene entry deserves a note.  Table 2 prints 0.2 wt % i-butene in the
    feed and 0 in BOTH products, which is impossible; record section 5.4 measures
    the discrepancy at -100 %.  The seed below therefore carries the feed's
    i-butene into the bottoms, purely so the guess conserves material.  That is
    a seeding choice with no source behind it, and it is exactly why the anchor
    rows are on the KEYS only.                                                */

componentMolarFlows
{
    propane          1.226951 kmol/h;      //  0.3 wt %, scaled to B = 310.687401
    isoButane        0.930861 kmol/h;      //  0.3 wt %
    nButane        304.387322 kmol/h;      // 98.1 wt %
    1Butene          0.321436 kmol/h;      //  0.1 wt %
    isoButene        0.934219 kmol/h;      //  see the note above -- a seed, not data
    trans2Butene     0.321436 kmol/h;      //  0.1 wt %
    neopentane       0.499927 kmol/h;      //  0.2 wt %
    isopentane       2.749599 kmol/h;      //  1.1 wt %
    nPentane         0.249964 kmol/h;      //  0.1 wt %
}

T               329.4 K;                   // guess, near the reboiler bubble point
P               658600 Pa;
vaporFraction   0.0;
